1
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:33,270
No!

2
00:01:34,830 --> 00:01:35,470
Valon!

3
00:01:36,470 --> 00:01:39,370
Can she even be revived after all that?

4
00:01:39,890 --> 00:01:43,370
I've heard that it's been done before, but...

5
00:01:43,370 --> 00:01:46,550
Hey, Laios? What are you...

6
00:01:46,550 --> 00:01:49,270
The Resurrection Office. They'll know what to do.

7
00:01:50,050 --> 00:01:51,870
Are you planning to take everything?

8
00:01:52,430 --> 00:01:54,310
But aren't Wargbones mixed in there, too?

9
00:01:54,830 --> 00:01:56,270
It's hard to tell them apart.

10
00:01:58,070 --> 00:01:58,970
Let me help.

11
00:01:59,990 --> 00:02:02,590
Please wait!

12
00:02:03,850 --> 00:02:06,990
The link between the soul and body is fragile now.

13
00:02:07,270 --> 00:02:08,430
You shouldn't move her.

14
00:02:09,210 --> 00:02:12,690
The more damaged the body is, the weaker the soul's bond.

15
00:02:13,170 --> 00:02:17,370
When a Resurrection fails, it's usually because the soul separated too far,

16
00:02:17,650 --> 00:02:19,810
or because the body wasn't fully restored.

17
00:02:20,490 --> 00:02:21,590
Then what should we do?

18
00:02:22,190 --> 00:02:25,810
We go get a Revival Specialist and revive her here.

19
00:02:25,810 --> 00:02:31,090
But the Restoration requires more than twice the amount of calories for the damaged parts,

20
00:02:31,310 --> 00:02:34,690
so we'd also need to bring a lot of fresh meat for it to work.

21
00:02:34,690 --> 00:02:37,190
It would rot on the way down, wouldn't it?

22
00:02:37,190 --> 00:02:37,850
Hang on.

23
00:02:37,850 --> 00:02:38,050
Huh?

24
00:02:38,850 --> 00:02:39,350
Yes.

25
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:43,810
We have a large amount of fresh meat right here in front of us.

26
00:02:43,810 --> 00:02:46,330
Hey, now hold on a sec.

27
00:02:46,630 --> 00:02:49,210
You're gonna resurrect her with Dragon Meat?

28
00:02:49,910 --> 00:02:51,710
Reviving isn't even your specialty.

29
00:02:51,710 --> 00:02:56,330
I didn't want to scare anyone, so I never mentioned it.

30
00:02:56,330 --> 00:03:02,190
What I specialize in is actually ancient magic, which is highly forbidden.

31
00:03:03,130 --> 00:03:08,210
Its use is frowned upon, but using it to revive Falon, it's our best option.

32
00:03:08,350 --> 00:03:08,850
Marcil!

33
00:03:08,850 --> 00:03:10,090
Black magic?

34
00:03:10,450 --> 00:03:11,530
That stuff is evil.

35
00:03:12,390 --> 00:03:14,310
Magic doesn't have morality.

36
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:19,490
Well, Lyos, it's your choice.

37
00:03:20,390 --> 00:03:21,510
Please do it, Marcil.

38
00:03:22,070 --> 00:03:24,150
Bring my sister back from the dead.

39
00:03:26,530 --> 00:03:27,530
All right, then.

40
00:03:27,870 --> 00:03:28,410
I'll try.

41
00:03:28,990 --> 00:03:30,330
Are you guys insane?

42
00:03:30,790 --> 00:03:32,550
Using Dragon Meat, of all things.

43
00:03:33,030 --> 00:03:35,630
Goat and pig are what people would normally use for this,

44
00:03:35,730 --> 00:03:37,170
but we don't have that right now.

45
00:03:37,370 --> 00:03:38,710
All right, let's start.

46
00:03:38,850 --> 00:03:56,490
First things first, I would like to put the body back in its original shape,

47
00:03:56,610 --> 00:03:58,630
so I'll start assembling her skeleton.

48
00:03:59,050 --> 00:04:00,090
That makes sense.

49
00:04:00,570 --> 00:04:02,330
I'm familiar with canine skeletons,

50
00:04:02,330 --> 00:04:05,130
so I'll work on putting the wargs together.

51
00:04:05,130 --> 00:04:10,450
That's kind of unnecessary, isn't it?

52
00:04:10,490 --> 00:04:13,510
Not if it helps us avoid missing something or making dumb mistakes!

53
00:04:15,730 --> 00:04:17,890
Humans have around 200 bones.

54
00:04:18,350 --> 00:04:21,470
Then we're looking at about 840 bones total.

55
00:04:21,890 --> 00:04:22,230
Huh?

56
00:04:22,430 --> 00:04:23,490
How do you know that?

57
00:04:24,450 --> 00:04:26,530
Dogs have around 320 bones,

58
00:04:26,650 --> 00:04:28,050
and there are two skulls here,

59
00:04:28,190 --> 00:04:29,210
so it's easy math.

60
00:04:29,790 --> 00:04:32,210
Let's start with the most recognizable ones.

61
00:04:32,910 --> 00:04:35,090
The rounder set is a human's ribcage,

62
00:04:35,290 --> 00:04:38,250
and the spine is directly connected to the ribs.

63
00:04:38,430 --> 00:04:39,730
Their curves don't look the same,

64
00:04:39,850 --> 00:04:41,070
so they're easy to tell apart.

65
00:04:41,630 --> 00:04:45,110
The toughest ones are the smaller bones from the hands and feet.

66
00:04:45,570 --> 00:04:48,130
Yeah, it's a lot harder to tell the difference.

67
00:04:48,130 --> 00:04:51,270
Let's start with the bigger pieces and work down.

68
00:04:52,010 --> 00:04:54,410
This piece that I'm holding is the ankle bone.

69
00:04:55,030 --> 00:04:56,430
Find the next biggest one,

70
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:58,770
then connect the two sides that line up,

71
00:04:58,970 --> 00:05:00,610
and the instep is complete.

72
00:05:01,950 --> 00:05:04,350
And then we have the bones from the hands.

73
00:05:04,730 --> 00:05:06,750
Let's arrange them starting with the fingers.

74
00:05:07,010 --> 00:05:07,710
I got it!

75
00:05:09,230 --> 00:05:10,410
Like this, right?

76
00:05:11,330 --> 00:05:12,330
So close.

77
00:05:12,890 --> 00:05:14,710
Actually, the longest metacarpal,

78
00:05:14,870 --> 00:05:16,030
despite what you might think,

79
00:05:16,030 --> 00:05:17,490
goes on the pointer finger.

80
00:05:18,130 --> 00:05:19,610
That just leaves us with the ones

81
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:21,310
that connect the fingers to the wrist.

82
00:05:27,030 --> 00:05:27,970
Hint, please!

83
00:05:28,090 --> 00:05:29,650
This isn't a game, Lyos!

84
00:05:33,230 --> 00:05:33,750
There.

85
00:05:34,810 --> 00:05:35,590
It's ready!

86
00:05:39,330 --> 00:05:40,710
How do I put this?

87
00:05:41,590 --> 00:05:43,270
What a beautiful skeleton.

88
00:05:43,710 --> 00:05:45,290
Not bad for some bones.

89
00:05:45,290 --> 00:05:47,250
Seems she had good calcium intake.

90
00:05:48,130 --> 00:05:50,850
This isn't going to revive the wargs, too, is it?

91
00:05:51,310 --> 00:05:53,590
Only human souls get bound to the dungeon.

92
00:05:54,190 --> 00:05:54,910
Because otherwise,

93
00:05:55,430 --> 00:05:57,790
this place would burst from all the monster souls.

94
00:05:57,790 --> 00:06:09,410
All right.

95
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:10,630
Here we go.

96
00:06:10,630 --> 00:06:10,650
Here we go.

97
00:06:10,650 --> 00:06:13,650
And you guys are moving.

98
00:06:18,430 --> 00:06:19,490
We will keep living.

99
00:06:19,910 --> 00:06:20,610
Here we go.

100
00:06:20,610 --> 00:06:21,030
Thank you.

101
00:06:21,030 --> 00:06:21,570
I don't care.

102
00:06:21,570 --> 00:06:22,010
Let's see.

103
00:06:22,010 --> 00:06:22,630
I don't think.

104
00:06:22,630 --> 00:06:22,690
I don't think.

105
00:06:23,350 --> 00:06:23,930
I don't think.

106
00:06:23,990 --> 00:06:24,050
I don't think.

107
00:06:26,150 --> 00:06:26,870
I don't think.

108
00:06:28,950 --> 00:06:29,730
Oh set.

109
00:06:29,730 --> 00:06:30,230
Marcelle!

110
00:06:45,310 --> 00:06:46,270
Marcelle!

111
00:06:48,870 --> 00:06:50,290
She just fainted.

112
00:06:51,190 --> 00:06:52,390
So what happened?

113
00:06:52,770 --> 00:06:53,870
Did it actually work?

114
00:06:59,730 --> 00:07:13,330
Fallon!

115
00:07:14,550 --> 00:07:16,350
Her airway's full of blood!

116
00:07:17,090 --> 00:07:18,710
All right, just cough it out.

117
00:07:19,850 --> 00:07:21,470
There, all good.

118
00:07:26,470 --> 00:07:27,030
Fallon.

119
00:07:29,730 --> 00:07:43,830
I'm glad you're safe.

120
00:07:46,590 --> 00:07:47,590
You're cold.

121
00:07:48,810 --> 00:07:50,410
Right! My armor, sorry.

122
00:07:50,730 --> 00:07:51,970
Let me go get you some clothes.

123
00:07:54,970 --> 00:07:56,370
Fallon, what's the matter?

124
00:07:57,670 --> 00:07:59,250
You're feeling okay, right?

125
00:08:00,690 --> 00:08:02,370
Good. I'm glad to hear it.

126
00:08:03,290 --> 00:08:03,570
Marcel.

127
00:08:04,630 --> 00:08:05,190
Marcel!

128
00:08:08,010 --> 00:08:09,110
How's Fallon?

129
00:08:09,770 --> 00:08:10,870
Alive and well.

130
00:08:11,690 --> 00:08:13,370
But she's still a bit disoriented.

131
00:08:19,730 --> 00:08:20,530
Fallon!

132
00:08:20,530 --> 00:08:20,810
Fallon!

133
00:08:20,810 --> 00:08:27,890
I'm so glad. Thank goodness.

134
00:08:29,450 --> 00:08:29,910
Marcel.

135
00:08:29,910 --> 00:08:30,090
Marcel.

136
00:08:38,090 --> 00:08:38,990
Chill, Chuck.

137
00:08:38,990 --> 00:08:40,510
How are you feeling?

138
00:08:41,790 --> 00:08:44,090
She's still kind of confused about this.

139
00:08:44,710 --> 00:08:49,890
All right. This guy here? His name's Senshi. He's been a big help during our journey.

140
00:08:50,890 --> 00:08:54,170
Good to meet you, Fallon. I've heard a lot about you.

141
00:08:55,550 --> 00:08:56,130
Senshi.

142
00:08:56,130 --> 00:09:06,690
Seems like a good time to start prepping a meal.

143
00:09:10,690 --> 00:09:16,830
Thank goodness. I was so worried, Fallon. I'm so happy. I bet everything worked out in the end.

144
00:09:16,830 --> 00:09:18,230
Uh, Marcel?

145
00:09:18,230 --> 00:09:18,790
Hmm?

146
00:09:18,790 --> 00:09:20,690
I can wash myself, you know?

147
00:09:21,170 --> 00:09:24,450
Yeah, but I wanted to make sure your skin was properly restored.

148
00:09:24,790 --> 00:09:25,850
That tickles!

149
00:09:27,290 --> 00:09:27,810
Yes.

150
00:09:28,510 --> 00:09:28,990
Good.

151
00:09:28,990 --> 00:09:32,390
Why is there a news here?

152
00:09:33,230 --> 00:09:37,570
That's the mark I got from tripping and hitting the edge of the stairs when I was a little kid.

153
00:09:37,690 --> 00:09:38,850
Oh, that's all?

154
00:09:40,190 --> 00:09:40,670
Marcel.

155
00:09:41,570 --> 00:09:43,550
You look even paler than I do.

156
00:09:44,050 --> 00:09:46,110
That's because I don't have any mana.

157
00:09:46,750 --> 00:09:49,450
If I eat something and get rest, I should be fi-

158
00:09:49,450 --> 00:09:51,250
Huh?

159
00:09:54,410 --> 00:09:55,950
What are you-

160
00:09:55,950 --> 00:09:59,390
Sorry if I scared you. I was trying to give you some of my mana.

161
00:09:59,770 --> 00:10:04,410
You don't have to do that. I don't even think you have enough to share with me right now, do you?

162
00:10:04,850 --> 00:10:10,050
I actually feel good. Like there's power welling deep inside of me.

163
00:10:11,230 --> 00:10:17,290
Fallon, you're still on the mend. So please, don't use magic until you're used to your body again.

164
00:10:20,030 --> 00:10:21,850
I died, didn't I?

165
00:10:21,850 --> 00:10:26,310
I... I don't really remember much about it.

166
00:10:27,510 --> 00:10:28,650
What happened exactly?

167
00:10:29,530 --> 00:10:31,810
You were all covered in wounds and...

168
00:10:31,810 --> 00:10:33,850
For the red dragon to appear here...

169
00:10:34,410 --> 00:10:36,190
Wait, are Shiro and Namaari okay?

170
00:10:36,770 --> 00:10:40,610
I would feel just awful if anyone risked their lives and got hurt because of me.

171
00:10:40,850 --> 00:10:42,090
No, they're all fine.

172
00:10:42,170 --> 00:10:45,850
Also, that magic circle I saw...

173
00:10:46,570 --> 00:10:49,430
There was something that just didn't feel right about it.

174
00:10:49,430 --> 00:10:55,870
I'm so sorry. It's all my fault you had to use something like that.

175
00:10:58,130 --> 00:10:59,110
Stop worrying!

176
00:11:00,850 --> 00:11:04,210
Sure, we ran into some hardships. Things got pretty rough.

177
00:11:04,630 --> 00:11:07,310
But it's easy to look back and laugh at all that now.

178
00:11:07,530 --> 00:11:09,570
Because everything turned out well in the end.

179
00:11:10,570 --> 00:11:13,610
Fallon, there's no need for you to blame yourself.

180
00:11:14,270 --> 00:11:16,710
No one regrets anything that we've been through.

181
00:11:16,710 --> 00:11:27,170
As for that magic circle, things will be fine if we erase it.

182
00:11:28,630 --> 00:11:30,090
For the moment...

183
00:11:30,090 --> 00:11:33,850
Our biggest concern is how to safely get back home.

184
00:11:34,370 --> 00:11:36,730
Oh! I still have to wash all my clothes.

185
00:11:36,910 --> 00:11:38,890
And we still have to find you a new outfit.

186
00:11:39,410 --> 00:11:41,670
Ugh, if it weren't for those stupid frogs.

187
00:11:42,230 --> 00:11:43,030
There were frogs?

188
00:11:43,030 --> 00:11:46,170
What do we do now?

189
00:11:47,310 --> 00:11:48,390
Return to the surface.

190
00:11:49,390 --> 00:11:52,050
We can't use return magic or the orcs' tunnels.

191
00:11:52,350 --> 00:11:54,650
So we'll have to get to the castle from the main road.

192
00:11:55,070 --> 00:11:55,910
Not what I meant.

193
00:11:56,650 --> 00:12:00,550
You may have rescued your sister, but the fact remains that we're still broke.

194
00:12:01,010 --> 00:12:03,190
I do have some savings in the bank, you know.

195
00:12:03,690 --> 00:12:05,230
But no promissory note.

196
00:12:05,750 --> 00:12:07,750
And it'll take a month to reproduce it.

197
00:12:07,750 --> 00:12:09,610
Yeah, you're right.

198
00:12:11,890 --> 00:12:15,090
So about that Marcel, the black magic she used.

199
00:12:15,230 --> 00:12:16,970
Did you already know she had that ability?

200
00:12:17,530 --> 00:12:19,510
I never asked her about the details.

201
00:12:19,930 --> 00:12:22,890
But she had mentioned wanting to go into a dungeon to study it.

202
00:12:23,250 --> 00:12:24,810
It always seemed weird to me.

203
00:12:25,390 --> 00:12:28,950
An elf who looked like she was living pretty comfy wanting to go into a dungeon.

204
00:12:29,490 --> 00:12:31,910
You don't suppose she's one of those dark elves, do you?

205
00:12:31,910 --> 00:12:35,690
I don't want her causing any problems for us.

206
00:12:36,190 --> 00:12:38,410
Who are you calling a dark elf?

207
00:12:40,050 --> 00:12:42,970
If dark magic was harmless, it wouldn't be forbidden.

208
00:12:43,530 --> 00:12:44,110
Oh yeah?

209
00:12:44,490 --> 00:12:46,470
So you'd consider healing magic harmless?

210
00:12:47,390 --> 00:12:49,210
Because even that can be used for torture.

211
00:12:49,210 --> 00:12:53,290
I'm researching ways that forbidden magic can be useful to people.

212
00:12:53,950 --> 00:12:55,890
And honestly, I'm not ashamed of it.

213
00:12:57,450 --> 00:13:02,470
Although I think it's for the best if we forget about the method of resurrection this time around, if that's okay.

214
00:13:02,710 --> 00:13:04,830
Didn't you just say that you weren't ashamed of it?

215
00:13:06,290 --> 00:13:07,210
It's fine.

216
00:13:07,430 --> 00:13:08,810
It's all over anyway.

217
00:13:09,650 --> 00:13:11,050
I just realized.

218
00:13:11,050 --> 00:13:18,670
Where'd Senshi go?

219
00:13:19,210 --> 00:13:20,650
Maybe dealing with the dragon meat?

220
00:13:21,170 --> 00:13:23,070
Oh, I just passed Mr. Senshi.

221
00:13:23,290 --> 00:13:25,510
He was carrying a giant pan along with firewood.

222
00:13:25,830 --> 00:13:28,070
Like I said, he's prepping food.

223
00:13:29,510 --> 00:13:30,030
Food?

224
00:13:30,970 --> 00:13:32,210
Near the dragon?

225
00:13:34,910 --> 00:13:36,290
We've got to stop him!

226
00:13:36,570 --> 00:13:37,310
What's happening?

227
00:13:37,590 --> 00:13:40,070
When I cut open the dragon, I cut the fuel organ.

228
00:13:40,070 --> 00:13:44,070
So lighting a fire close to it is gonna...

229
00:13:44,070 --> 00:13:44,850
Senshi!

230
00:13:45,490 --> 00:13:47,110
Please, stop!

231
00:14:05,030 --> 00:14:07,110
He... he's alive.

232
00:14:07,430 --> 00:14:09,370
Is this defensive magic?

233
00:14:10,070 --> 00:14:16,030
Falon, did you cast that?

234
00:14:16,690 --> 00:14:17,730
I think so.

235
00:14:17,770 --> 00:14:20,310
How'd you do it so fast and without chanting?

236
00:14:21,150 --> 00:14:22,250
I don't know.

237
00:14:22,850 --> 00:14:24,850
I thought about needing to protect everyone.

238
00:14:25,230 --> 00:14:26,310
And then...

239
00:14:26,310 --> 00:14:28,010
That's amazing.

240
00:14:28,550 --> 00:14:30,450
Is this that sudden heroic strength thing?

241
00:14:31,070 --> 00:14:34,230
Sure would have been real helpful to have when we were fighting the red dragon.

242
00:14:34,230 --> 00:14:40,350
Anyway, you were revived not that long ago, so please, refrain from using any more magic.

243
00:14:41,310 --> 00:14:42,610
That startled me.

244
00:14:43,030 --> 00:14:46,250
Didn't I say that dragons breathe fire from fuel they produce?

245
00:14:46,750 --> 00:14:48,070
You ignited that fuel.

246
00:14:48,930 --> 00:14:50,310
It's not going out, huh?

247
00:14:50,310 --> 00:14:52,310
The fat inside the body is burning.

248
00:14:52,310 --> 00:14:54,310
It'll die down eventually.

249
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:57,970
If that's the case, then I can't take the meat from in there.

250
00:14:57,970 --> 00:15:00,090
Hmm, not good.

251
00:15:00,090 --> 00:15:05,430
I guess I'll use that fire to cook.

252
00:15:05,430 --> 00:15:10,190
Mix flour, yeast, salt, and water in a bowl and knead well.

253
00:15:10,810 --> 00:15:12,090
Let it rest for a bit.

254
00:15:12,470 --> 00:15:14,150
Go take a bath while it rests.

255
00:15:15,090 --> 00:15:17,190
Shape it to your lichen as you stretch it out.

256
00:15:17,670 --> 00:15:19,330
And add your choice of toppings.

257
00:15:20,150 --> 00:15:22,830
Lightly sprinkle flour onto a piece of dragon hide.

258
00:15:22,830 --> 00:15:25,470
Then place it inside the dragon.

259
00:15:26,710 --> 00:15:28,810
Cut off the tip of the dragon's tail.

260
00:15:29,070 --> 00:15:30,770
Ah, that's so wasteful!

261
00:15:31,070 --> 00:15:33,250
Now skin it and place it in a soup.

262
00:15:33,830 --> 00:15:35,730
Cut the meat into a block shape.

263
00:15:36,370 --> 00:15:41,410
Place it on a heated scale, and after both sides are seared, dip it into some seasoning.

264
00:15:46,270 --> 00:15:47,170
It's ready.

265
00:15:51,670 --> 00:15:52,610
Oh, man.

266
00:15:52,830 --> 00:15:53,830
Looks delicious.

267
00:15:55,590 --> 00:15:56,870
Is this okay to eat?

268
00:15:56,990 --> 00:15:58,230
Of course it isn't!

269
00:16:08,410 --> 00:16:08,810
Tasty!

270
00:16:09,530 --> 00:16:11,950
Feels like the first good meal I've eaten in a while.

271
00:16:12,190 --> 00:16:12,970
Good, good.

272
00:16:13,110 --> 00:16:14,690
Take your revenge on that dragon.

273
00:16:15,070 --> 00:16:16,590
I guess it's fine.

274
00:16:16,890 --> 00:16:18,570
I'm just glad that she's feeling better.

275
00:16:22,830 --> 00:16:28,570
It's pretty tough.

276
00:16:28,810 --> 00:16:30,490
The flavor seems kind of familiar.

277
00:16:30,830 --> 00:16:32,650
Yeah, I can't really place it.

278
00:16:33,050 --> 00:16:34,970
I don't think it's cow or pig, though.

279
00:16:35,490 --> 00:16:38,090
If anything, it kind of tastes like...

280
00:16:38,090 --> 00:16:40,730
It's a bit like living armor, isn't it?

281
00:16:40,770 --> 00:16:41,850
Huh, you think so?

282
00:16:41,850 --> 00:16:44,730
I don't taste the same rusty tinge the armor had.

283
00:16:45,310 --> 00:16:49,410
The Kelpie and Frog were pretty soft, so maybe it's more like the basilisk?

284
00:16:50,010 --> 00:16:51,450
What do you think, Lyos?

285
00:16:51,450 --> 00:16:56,750
What are you all even talking about?

286
00:16:56,850 --> 00:16:58,050
This color!

287
00:16:58,590 --> 00:16:59,790
This firm texture!

288
00:17:00,530 --> 00:17:01,610
The rich flavor!

289
00:17:02,110 --> 00:17:04,130
Each of these things are distinctly unique!

290
00:17:04,130 --> 00:17:07,970
So why are you comparing the taste of this to anything else?

291
00:17:08,770 --> 00:17:11,510
Because this is the flavor of a dragon!

292
00:17:16,790 --> 00:17:21,390
Uh, uh, Fallon, you may have realized by now, but...

293
00:17:21,390 --> 00:17:25,050
We haven't had the resources to buy food, so we've been eating monsters...

294
00:17:25,050 --> 00:17:28,090
So cool!

295
00:17:28,710 --> 00:17:30,570
That is so cool!

296
00:17:30,570 --> 00:17:34,350
What kind of monsters did you eat, and how did you eat them? Tell me!

297
00:17:34,970 --> 00:17:36,030
Worried for nothing.

298
00:17:36,610 --> 00:17:38,270
This is the worst possible outcome!

299
00:17:38,750 --> 00:17:40,410
We ate a scorpion and a slime.

300
00:17:41,210 --> 00:17:42,810
Even a walking mushroom.

301
00:17:43,110 --> 00:17:44,150
No way! You did?

302
00:17:44,690 --> 00:17:47,370
We harvested vegetables from some golems, too.

303
00:17:47,790 --> 00:17:49,870
Wow! You ate a fish, man?

304
00:17:50,390 --> 00:17:52,590
That wasn't... an option.

305
00:17:53,010 --> 00:17:54,750
We did eat some living armor, though.

306
00:17:54,790 --> 00:17:56,410
Huh? How'd you do that?

307
00:17:56,970 --> 00:17:57,770
Let's see.

308
00:17:58,110 --> 00:18:00,530
The armor is basically the outer shell.

309
00:18:00,570 --> 00:18:03,610
And then, inside is a mollusk colony, which...

310
00:18:03,610 --> 00:18:06,190
Wouldn't it be a lot faster to show her the real thing?

311
00:18:09,270 --> 00:18:09,670
Huh?

312
00:18:09,890 --> 00:18:11,030
What's this about?

313
00:18:11,130 --> 00:18:11,290
Shh!

314
00:18:14,110 --> 00:18:14,470
Huh?

315
00:18:17,710 --> 00:18:18,190
Laius!

316
00:18:18,330 --> 00:18:19,730
Why'd you keep this from us?

317
00:18:19,850 --> 00:18:20,850
I'm so sorry.

318
00:18:21,330 --> 00:18:23,030
Oh, adorable.

319
00:18:23,490 --> 00:18:24,310
Can I touch?

320
00:18:24,310 --> 00:18:29,570
Oh, it went back in.

321
00:18:29,570 --> 00:18:34,910
It moves around on its own.

322
00:18:35,190 --> 00:18:35,630
Seriously?

323
00:18:36,830 --> 00:18:37,310
Sorry.

324
00:18:38,130 --> 00:18:41,390
It was only supposed to tide me over until I found another weapon.

325
00:18:41,830 --> 00:18:44,450
But it reacts to other monsters, which is convenient.

326
00:18:45,110 --> 00:18:47,330
You were oddly perceptive at times.

327
00:18:47,450 --> 00:18:49,530
Should have had Nomari appraise it for us.

328
00:18:49,630 --> 00:18:53,550
In that situation, I probably would have also thought to hold onto it.

329
00:18:53,550 --> 00:18:59,030
But tell everyone next time, if you lose the trust of those around you, you lose everything.

330
00:18:59,830 --> 00:19:01,110
I won't do it again.

331
00:19:01,470 --> 00:19:02,470
You have my word.

332
00:19:02,770 --> 00:19:03,230
All right.

333
00:19:03,410 --> 00:19:04,570
So what's your plan now?

334
00:19:04,570 --> 00:19:07,150
I'd like to keep it until I get another weapon.

335
00:19:07,690 --> 00:19:10,030
I can kill it if I submerge it in water.

336
00:19:10,030 --> 00:19:14,150
But I'd have to break the sword to get it out, or it would just rot in there.

337
00:19:14,470 --> 00:19:15,310
That's not good.

338
00:19:15,550 --> 00:19:16,950
Guess we'll keep an eye on it.

339
00:19:17,570 --> 00:19:20,350
Aren't you the one who said monsters are dangerous creatures?

340
00:19:21,490 --> 00:19:23,850
And trust me, I haven't forgotten about that.

341
00:19:24,210 --> 00:19:28,510
I figured after I'd made it harmless, I could just go on and use it however I felt like.

342
00:19:28,510 --> 00:19:30,350
Well, I guess I was wrong.

343
00:19:30,950 --> 00:19:33,490
It's too difficult to use monsters while they're still alive.

344
00:19:34,550 --> 00:19:36,070
What does it taste like, brother?

345
00:19:36,670 --> 00:19:37,830
Do you want to eat it?

346
00:19:38,430 --> 00:19:39,290
Yes, please.

347
00:19:39,370 --> 00:19:40,070
I'd love that.

348
00:19:46,370 --> 00:19:50,730
There's doors all over this place, but seems like only two of them lead outside, huh?

349
00:19:51,070 --> 00:19:52,550
No getting ambushed, at least.

350
00:19:52,550 --> 00:19:59,970
This house seems like it'll be comfortable to live in.

351
00:20:00,150 --> 00:20:02,130
Why do they have seven bathrooms, though?

352
00:20:02,730 --> 00:20:04,270
All right, let's sleep here, then.

353
00:20:04,430 --> 00:20:04,830
Yay!

354
00:20:05,450 --> 00:20:08,230
It's been ages since I've slept in a real bed.

355
00:20:08,270 --> 00:20:10,370
We still gotta use our sleeping bags, you know.

356
00:20:17,570 --> 00:20:19,730
I'm sorry to be intruding like this.

357
00:20:19,730 --> 00:20:22,850
Once we get enough rest, then we'll be on our way.

358
00:20:23,470 --> 00:20:24,410
Hey, what's up?

359
00:20:25,090 --> 00:20:25,770
A resident.

360
00:20:26,410 --> 00:20:27,510
She's letting us stay.

361
00:20:28,210 --> 00:20:29,230
Is that so?

362
00:20:29,730 --> 00:20:30,510
That's great.

363
00:20:32,070 --> 00:20:35,610
There are only four of them, so we'll have to share a sleeping bag.

364
00:20:35,870 --> 00:20:39,390
We haven't really slept in the same bed since our school days, have we?

365
00:20:39,450 --> 00:20:40,830
I wonder if we'll both fit.

366
00:20:41,710 --> 00:20:44,810
I feel like I've probably gotten a lot taller since then, huh?

367
00:20:44,970 --> 00:20:46,870
Oh, don't be so ridiculous!

368
00:20:46,870 --> 00:20:52,690
I don't care if you've grown, you're still a runt in my eyes.

369
00:20:56,830 --> 00:20:58,710
I'm glad that you're with us again.

370
00:21:00,350 --> 00:21:01,410
Yeah, me too.

371
00:21:04,730 --> 00:21:06,750
I'm gonna go say goodnight to my brother.

372
00:21:11,430 --> 00:21:11,830
Brother?

373
00:21:11,830 --> 00:21:14,190
What is it?

374
00:21:22,390 --> 00:21:23,630
This injury here.

375
00:21:24,230 --> 00:21:25,270
You were being reckless.

376
00:21:25,990 --> 00:21:26,830
Why would you do...

377
00:21:27,530 --> 00:21:36,610
Maybe if a certain sister of mine hadn't been reckless first, I wouldn't have even had that injury.

378
00:21:36,970 --> 00:21:37,330
Huh?

379
00:21:37,330 --> 00:21:40,150
So don't ever do anything like that again.

380
00:21:40,630 --> 00:21:43,330
I honestly can't say I even recall what I...

381
00:21:45,330 --> 00:21:51,510
I won't do it again.

382
00:21:55,010 --> 00:21:56,950
Goodnight, big brother.

383
00:21:57,810 --> 00:21:58,670
You too.

384
00:21:59,210 --> 00:21:59,810
Sleep tight.

385
00:22:01,330 --> 00:22:02,250
Huh?

386
00:22:02,250 --> 00:22:03,390
You too.

387
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:33,370
Thank you.

